<v Helen> Sarah did one last year ...


48
00:05:25,207 --> 00:05:26,075
<v Brad> Who’s she?


49
00:05:26,075 --> 00:05:30,730
<v Helen> She’s doing the same option as me on marketing. I’ll ask her advice on what to include.


50
00:05:30,730 --> 00:05:36,249
<v Brad> Great. So that just leaves the bibliography at the end. I suppose it’ll mainly be articles.


51
00:05:36,249 --> 00:05:40,999
<v Helen> Yeah. So we’ll just look on the web ... and we can leave that till later.


52
00:05:40,999 --> 00:05:43,815
<v Brad> But we’ve been advised against that ...


53
00:05:43,815 --> 00:05:47,528
<v Helen> Well, we could have a look through some journals in the library.


54
00:05:47,528 --> 00:05:52,560
<v Brad> I think we should start by looking through module handbooks. I think that’ll give us some good leads.


